ve re-runs; all analysis provenance is in `manifest.json`. Then phase 2 (practice controller: stem muting, loop/tempo management, take recording) builds on the same manifest and the same `[vgt]` track conventions.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:6:in the `llm-wiki` vault; the LALAL.AI REST API v1\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:7:(`https://www.lalal.ai/api/v1/docs/`, OpenAPI specification at\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:8:`https://www.lalal.ai/api/v1/openapi.json`); and vgt's existing sidecar /\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:16:**Scope decision (2026-07-20): LALAL.AI is the sole separation backend.**\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:23:manual LALAL workflow exactly — **no instrument probing, no configurable stem\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:53:- LALAL.AI is the cloud default; it exposes dedicated **acoustic-** and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:55:  for a practice workflow. This is the decisive reason to build on LALAL.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:62:- Design rule that still applies: evaluate every stem for **interference and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:65:- Resilience caveat: LALAL is subscription-gated. With no offline fallback,\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:70:**From LALAL API v1:**\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:108:(returning that stem and a back track), the recipe maps onto LALAL as:\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:174:  HTTP/LALAL details while allowing a fake backend to exercise the same retry\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:175:  and resume logic. Only `LalalSeparator` is implemented now.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:176:- **Light dependency**: LALAL needs only an HTTP client (`httpx` or `requests`)\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:255:  backend_state, status, outputs, completed_at, error}`. LALAL backend state\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:264:### B — LALAL API v1 backend (priority:high, L)\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:268:  from **`LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`** and is never persisted or logged.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:299:  checkpo